  "behavior_implemented": [
    "Discovery is no longer minted from package bytes, install state, registry state, expected identity, or caller-written discovery documents. Caller documents and registry-visible substitutions fail closed; the supported-host discovery adapter only accepts an independently observed supported-host route and currently returns ObjectUnavailable when that observation cannot be exercised.",
    "Registry observation remains AppRegistry-only and AppRegistry promotion remains tied to confined file provenance rather than arbitrary caller-owned bytes.",
    "Runtime plans are issued only through the installed supported runtime route: the executable must be the exact package entry runtime/runtime-probe-bin, match the install snapshot, match the supported host capability, and revalidate after execution. Legacy RuntimeProbePlan::new is fail-closed for direct caller-selected binaries.",
    "Package artifact transactions retain the publication postimage and rollback now revalidates the original transaction root, output path, journey binding, current postimage, and object identities before writing.",
    "Focused controls cover registry-present/discovery-absent substitution, caller-authored discovery documents, arbitrary runtime echo scripts, sibling/wrong runtime executable routes, replacement executables, same-package cross-journey package publication transplant, and rollback cross-root/path/journey transplants.",
    "Historical supported-package WorkerResult fixture verification now withholds the stale R3 artifact claim when its referenced root-owned artifacts are absent in this refreshed branch."
  ],
